window.docContents[180].resolve({"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subsumption-Rule":{"contents":"τ₂\nOur goal for this chapter is to add subtyping to the simply typed\nlambda-calculus (with some basic extensions). This involves two steps:\n\n* Defining a binary subtype relation between types.* Enriching the typing relation to take subtyping into account.\n\nThe second step is actually very simple.  We add just a single rule\nto the typing relation: the so-called rule of subsumption:\n\n                         Γ ⊢ t₁ ⦂ τ₁     τ₁ <: τ₂\n                         --------------------------           (sub)\n                               Γ ⊢ t₁ ⦂ τ₂\n\n\nThis rule says, intuitively, that it is OK to \"forget\" some of\nwhat we know about a term.\n\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009Sub: Subtyping\u0009Concepts","header":"8.1.3. The Subsumption Rule","id":"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subsumption-Rule"}});